    <bpmn:process id="W_W496" name="W496. Customer Loyalty Fraud Detection &amp; Prevention" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Fraud alert from loyalty system analytics; anomaly detection threshold breach; customer complaint investigation; manual tip-off from store staff
Frequency: Weekly (automated scanning); event-driven (investigation activation); monthly (reporting)
Volume: ~50–100 flagged cases/month for review; ~5–15 confirmed fraud cases/month
Owner: Marketing — Loyalty Program Manager
Participants: LP Analyst, IT Security, Customer Service, Store Manager, Finance — Payment Settlement
Source: workflow W496 — Customer Loyalty Fraud Detection &amp; Prevention</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W496_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W496_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W496_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W496_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W496_Lane2" name="Loyalty Program Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W496_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W496_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W496_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W496_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W496_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W496_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W496_Start4" name="Fraud alert from loyalty system analytics; anomaly detection threshold breach; customer…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W496_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W496_Task5" name="Automated Fraud Scanning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Automated Fraud Scanning: Loyalty system runs automated fraud detection rules weekly: (a) Velocity rules: accounts earning or redeeming points at abnormal rates (e.g., &gt;10x average member activity in 24 hours); (b) Pattern rules: multiple accounts sharing same device, IP address, or phone number; (c) Return-points mismatch: accounts with high return rates but retained points; (d) Geographic anomaly: points earned at a store the member has never visited, or at multiple distant stores on the same day; (e) Employee-linked accounts: accounts linked to employee IDs (W205) showing unusual point accumulation; (f) flagged cases are queued for manual review
Responsible (R): System / Loyalty Program Manager
Accountable (A): IT Security
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W496_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W496_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W496_Task6" name="Case Triage">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Case Triage: Loyalty Program Manager reviews flagged cases: (a) classify case severity: High (employee involvement, organized ring, financial impact &gt;PHP 10,000), Medium (individual fraud, PHP 1,000–10,000 impact), Low (suspicious but possibly legitimate activity); (b) assign investigation priority; (c) for High severity: escalate to LP Analyst (W466) for cross-functional investigation; (d) for Medium/Low: Loyalty Program Manager investigates directly
Responsible (R): Loyalty Program Manager
Accountable (A): Marketing Director
Duration: 4 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W496_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W496_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W496_Task7" name="Investigation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Investigation: Loyalty Program Manager investigates flagged cases: (a) review account activity log: all point earn/redeem transactions, linked devices, store visits, purchase history; (b) cross-reference with POS transaction data (W5B) — verify that purchases generating points actually occurred; (c) cross-reference with returns data (W12A) — verify points reversal on returned items; (d) for employee-linked accounts: cross-reference with employee work schedule (W34) — are they at the store when points are earned?; (e) for account takeover: review login logs (device, IP, location, timestamp); (f) document findings in fraud case file
Responsible (R): Loyalty Program Manager / LP Analyst
Accountable (A): Marketing Director
Duration: 1–3 hours/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W496_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W496_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W496_Task8" name="Fraud Confirmation &amp; Action">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Fraud Confirmation &amp; Action: For confirmed fraud cases: (a) Account takeover: reset account credentials, freeze points balance, notify affected member via customer service (W258), restore stolen points; (b) Points farming / fake accounts: deactivate fraudulent accounts, forfeit all points, block device/IP; (c) Return-points arbitrage: correct points balance (reverse unearned points), update system to auto-reverse points on all returns; (d) Employee-assisted fraud: escalate to LP (W466) and HR for disciplinary action (W72/W43); recover fraudulent points; (e) Promotional abuse: close loophole (coordinate with IT per W132), forfeit fraudulently earned points; (f) for all cases: document action taken and update fraud prevention rules
Responsible (R): Loyalty Program Manager
Accountable (A): Marketing Director / LP Director
Duration: 1–2 hours/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W496_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W496_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W496_Task9" name="System Rule Enhancement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: System Rule Enhancement: Based on fraud patterns identified, Loyalty Program Manager updates fraud detection rules: (a) add new rules to automated scanning engine (W496.1); (b) adjust velocity thresholds based on legitimate vs. fraudulent activity patterns; (c) coordinate with IT to implement system-level controls: mandatory points reversal on returns, CAPTCHA for online enrollment (W263), device fingerprinting for account access, employee account tagging (W205); (d) submit rule changes through change management (W132)
Responsible (R): Loyalty Program Manager / IT
Accountable (A): Marketing Director
Duration: Event-driven</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W496_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W496_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W496_Task10" name="Monthly Fraud Report">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Monthly Fraud Report: Loyalty Program Manager prepares monthly loyalty fraud report: (a) total flagged cases, confirmed fraud cases, and false positive rate; (b) fraud loss quantification (points fraudulently earned/redeemed × PHP 1.00/point); (c) fraud type breakdown (account takeover, points farming, return arbitrage, employee-assisted, promotional abuse); (d) recovery actions taken; (e) rule enhancements implemented; (f) fraud trend analysis (increasing/decreasing by type); (g) update loyalty program financial liability estimate (W104) to reflect fraud adjustments
Responsible (R): Loyalty Program Manager
Accountable (A): Marketing Director
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W496_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W496_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W496_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W496_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W496_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-187 (ensure marketing spend &amp; loyalty-fraud control.) | - operational: analysis that may not be available in real-time
Owner: Marketing — Loyalty Program Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W496_Assoc13" sourceRef="W496_Annotation12" targetRef="W496_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W496_Flow14" sourceRef="W496_Start4" targetRef="W496_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W496_Flow15" sourceRef="W496_Task5" targetRef="W496_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W496_Flow16" sourceRef="W496_Task6" targetRef="W496_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W496_Flow17" sourceRef="W496_Task7" targetRef="W496_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W496_Flow18" sourceRef="W496_Task8" targetRef="W496_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W496_Flow19" sourceRef="W496_Task9" targetRef="W496_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W496_Flow20" sourceRef="W496_Task10" targetRef="W496_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
