    <bpmn:process id="W_W565" name="W565. Marketing Campaign ROI &amp; Attribution Analysis" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Campaign completion (per W83 campaign lifecycle); monthly campaign portfolio review; quarterly executive review
Frequency: ~4–6 active campaigns at any time; monthly analysis cycle; quarterly executive presentation
Volume: ~50–60 campaign-channel instances per year (from W83&#x27;s ~23–34 campaigns) across channels (digital, print, in-store, radio, TV, outdoor); ~PHP 300–500M annual marketing spend
Owner: Marketing Analytics Manager / VP Marketing
Participants: Marketing Analytics Manager, VP Marketing, Digital Marketing Specialist (C for digital data), Category Manager (C for sales impact), Finance Analyst (C for margin analysis), Agency Account Manager (C for media data)
Source: workflow W565 — Marketing Campaign ROI &amp; Attribution Analysis</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W565_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W565_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W565_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W565_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W565_Lane2" name="Marketing Analytics Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W565_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W565_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W565_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W565_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W565_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W565_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W565_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W565_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W565_Task18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W565_Lane3" name="Finance Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W565_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W565_Lane4" name="VP Marketing">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W565_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W565_End19</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W565_Start6" name="Campaign completion (per W83 campaign lifecycle); monthly campaign portfolio review…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W565_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W565_Task7" name="Campaign completion trigger from W83 (campaign manager marks campaign as…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Campaign completion trigger from W83 (campaign manager marks campaign as &quot;Completed&quot;); system creates ROI analysis task with campaign metadata (channels, dates, budget, KPIs)
Responsible (R): System / Marketing Analytics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W565_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W565_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W565_Task8" name="Campaign data collection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Campaign data collection: Marketing Analytics Manager gathers: (a) Spend data by channel and tactic from agency invoices and platform dashboards; (b) Reach/impression data from media platforms (Facebook Ads Manager, Google Ads, TV ratings, radio listenership); (c) Engagement data: clicks, video views, social interactions; (d) Conversion data: e-commerce sales attributed to campaign (UTM tracking), in-store sales lift (matching campaign period vs. baseline), coupon/barcode redemptions per W539; (e) New customer acquisition: loyalty enrollments attributed to campaign per W551
Responsible (R): Marketing Analytics Manager / Digital Marketing Specialist
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 4–6 hours/campaign</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W565_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W565_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W565_Task9" name="Sales lift analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Sales lift analysis: compare category sales during campaign period vs. pre-campaign baseline (4-week average); control for seasonality and external factors (typhoons, holidays, competitor promotions)
Responsible (R): Marketing Analytics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 2–3 hours/campaign</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W565_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W565_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W565_Task10" name="Attribution modeling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Attribution modeling: apply multi-touch attribution model — (a) First-touch: channel that first introduced customer to campaign; (b) Last-touch: channel directly preceding purchase; (c) Linear: equal credit across all touchpoints; (d) Time-decay: more credit to touchpoints closer to conversion
Responsible (R): Marketing Analytics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 3–4 hours/campaign</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W565_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W565_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W565_Task11" name="Channel ROI calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Channel ROI calculation: (Revenue attributed to channel – Spend) / Spend × 100; calculate ROI for each channel and tactic
Responsible (R): Marketing Analytics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 1 hour/campaign</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W565_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W565_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W565_Task12" name="Campaign ROI calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Campaign ROI calculation: (Incremental revenue – Total campaign cost including COGS impact of discounts) / Total campaign cost × 100; includes Category Manager input on margin impact and inventory sell-through per W57
Responsible (R): Marketing Analytics Manager / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 2 hours/campaign</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W565_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W565_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W565_Task13" name="Customer lifetime value impact">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Customer lifetime value impact: assess whether campaign-acquired customers have higher repeat purchase rates per W156 (CDP); calculate 90-day and 180-day repeat rate for campaign-acquired vs. organic customers
Responsible (R): Marketing Analytics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 2 hours/campaign</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W565_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W565_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W565_Task14" name="Finance Analyst validates margin calculations and ensures discount costs are…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Finance Analyst validates margin calculations and ensures discount costs are properly allocated to campaign cost (not buried in COGS)
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 1 hour/campaign</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W565_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W565_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W565_Task15" name="Monthly campaign portfolio report">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Monthly campaign portfolio report: ROI by campaign, by channel, by category; top 5 performing campaigns; bottom 5 underperformers; year-to-date cumulative ROI
Responsible (R): Marketing Analytics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 4–6 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W565_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W565_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W565_Task16" name="Quarterly executive review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Quarterly executive review: VP Marketing presents to CMO and CFO — budget allocation effectiveness, channel mix optimization, campaign frequency optimization; includes budget reallocation recommendation for next quarter
Responsible (R): VP Marketing / Marketing Analytics Manager
Accountable (A): CMO / CFO
Duration: 8–10 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W565_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W565_Flow32</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W565_Task17" name="Budget reallocation recommendation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 11: Budget reallocation recommendation: shift spend from underperforming channels to high-ROI channels for next quarter; feed into W26 (annual budget preparation)
Responsible (R): Marketing Analytics Manager / VP Marketing
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 2 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W565_Flow32</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W565_Flow33</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W565_Task18" name="Annual marketing ROI benchmark">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 12: Annual marketing ROI benchmark: compare BuildRight marketing efficiency vs. Philippine retail industry benchmarks; present annual marketing effectiveness report feeding into W26
Responsible (R): Marketing Analytics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 16 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W565_Flow33</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W565_Flow34</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W565_End19" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W565_Flow34</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W565_Annotation20">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-187 (ensure marketing spend &amp; loyalty-fraud control.) | - operational: Marketing Analytics Manager / VP Marketing review and approval gate
Owner: Marketing Analytics Manager / VP Marketing</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W565_Assoc21" sourceRef="W565_Annotation20" targetRef="W565_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W565_Flow22" sourceRef="W565_Start6" targetRef="W565_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W565_Flow23" sourceRef="W565_Task7" targetRef="W565_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W565_Flow24" sourceRef="W565_Task8" targetRef="W565_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W565_Flow25" sourceRef="W565_Task9" targetRef="W565_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W565_Flow26" sourceRef="W565_Task10" targetRef="W565_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W565_Flow27" sourceRef="W565_Task11" targetRef="W565_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W565_Flow28" sourceRef="W565_Task12" targetRef="W565_Task13" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W565_Flow29" sourceRef="W565_Task13" targetRef="W565_Task14" />
