    <bpmn:process id="W_W1259" name="W1259. Trade Professional Community Building, Retention Program &amp; Contractor Loyalty Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Scheduled — monthly community event planning; quarterly retention analysis; ad-hoc triggered by trade account churn alert or competitor trade program launch
Frequency: Monthly community engagement activities; quarterly retention analysis and program review; annual program strategy refresh
Volume: ~5,000 active trade account customers; ~200 corporate account customers; monthly community events at top 50 stores
Owner: Trade Marketing Manager
Participants: Category Manager, Store Manager, Sales Associate (Trade Desk), VP Merchandising, CMO
Source: workflow W1259 — Trade Professional Community Building, Retention Program &amp; Contractor Loyalty Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1259_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1259_Lane1" name="Trade Marketing Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1259_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1259_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1259_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1259_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1259_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1259_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1259_Start3" name="Scheduled — monthly community event planning; quarterly retention analysis; ad-hoc…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1259_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1259_Task4" name="Monthly trade community event execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly trade community event execution: Trade Marketing Manager coordinates monthly community events at top 50 stores (by trade revenue): (a) event types rotate: (i) product knowledge session (new tile installation techniques, electrical code updates), (ii) supplier demo day (power tool manufacturer demonstrates new products), (iii) business skills workshop (basic accounting for contractors, estimating techniques), (iv) networking mixer (connect contractors with developers/architects); (b) partner with suppliers for co-funding — supplier provides product samples, technical trainers, and promotional pricing during event; (c) target attendance: 20–30 trade professionals per event; (d) track attendance via loyalty card scan at event check-in
Responsible (R): Trade Marketing Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 8 hours/event (planning + execution)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1259_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1259_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1259_Task5" name="Trade customer retention analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Trade customer retention analytics: Monthly churn risk analysis: (a) identify trade accounts with declining monthly purchases (&gt; 20% decline vs. 3-month average); (b) flag accounts approaching credit limit exhaustion — may indicate financial distress or competitor shift; (c) calculate trade account lifetime value (LTV) and segment by risk tier: (i) green (active, growing), (ii) yellow (declining, at-risk), (iii) red (churned — no purchase in 60 days); (d) for yellow/red accounts: assign personal outreach from Store Manager or the dedicated Sales Associate (Trade Desk); (e) track retention rate by region and store
Responsible (R): Trade Marketing Manager / BI Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1259_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1259_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1259_Task6" name="Quarterly retention program review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Quarterly retention program review: Trade Marketing Manager reviews program effectiveness: (a) community event attendance trend — growing or declining?; (b) retention rate: % of trade accounts retained quarter-over-quarter; (c) trade revenue growth vs. non-trade revenue; (d) competitor intelligence: new trade programs launched by competitors; (e) customer feedback from trade community surveys; (f) adjust program elements: benefits, events, communication frequency based on data
Responsible (R): Trade Marketing Manager
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1259_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1259_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1259_Task7" name="Annual trade loyalty program enhancement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Annual trade loyalty program enhancement: Annual strategy refresh: (a) review trade loyalty tier structure — are the tier thresholds (Bronze, Silver, Gold, Platinum per W17) appropriate for trade customers?; (b) evaluate new benefits: (i) priority loading at lumber yard, (ii) dedicated trade phone line for orders, (iii) extended credit terms for top-tier, (iv) annual trade appreciation gala; (c) benchmark against Philippine and international trade programs (Home Depot Pro, Ace Trade); (d) propose program changes and budget to CMO and VP Merchandising
Responsible (R): Trade Marketing Manager
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 16 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1259_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1259_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1259_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1259_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1259_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-281 (ensure controlled execution — Campaign Planning &amp; Execution (PA-14.1).) | - operational: Trade Marketing Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Trade Marketing Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
