    <bpmn:process id="W_W1260" name="W1260. In-Store DIY Workshop &amp; Community Event Calendar Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Scheduled — monthly workshop calendar planning; quarterly workshop content review; ad-hoc triggered by seasonal merchandise push, supplier partnership opportunity, or store opening event
Frequency: Monthly calendar publication; weekly workshops at top 50 stores; quarterly content refresh
Volume: ~350 workshops per month across 200 stores (weekly at top 50 stores, monthly at remaining per the Frequency); ~5,250–7,000 attendees per month chain-wide
Owner: Marketing Events Coordinator
Participants: Store Manager, Sales Associate (presenter), Category Manager, Supplier Representative, VP Marketing, Content Manager
Source: workflow W1260 — In-Store DIY Workshop &amp; Community Event Calendar Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1260_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1260_Lane1" name="Marketing Events Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1260_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1260_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1260_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1260_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1260_Lane2" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1260_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1260_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1260_Start4" name="Scheduled — monthly workshop calendar planning; quarterly workshop content review; ad-hoc…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1260_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1260_Task5" name="Quarterly workshop content planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Quarterly workshop content planning: Marketing Events Coordinator plans quarterly workshop content calendar: (a) align workshops to seasonal merchandise calendar — Q1: painting techniques (post-holiday renovation), Q2: garden &amp; outdoor projects (summer), Q3: waterproofing &amp; flood control prep (rainy season), Q4: holiday décor &amp; lighting (Christmas); (b) develop 4–6 workshop templates per quarter: title, learning objectives, materials list, step-by-step project guide, estimated duration (60–90 min), maximum attendees (15–20); (c) partner with suppliers for co-branded workshops: paint manufacturer for painting workshop, tile supplier for tiling demo, power tool brand for tool skills workshop; (d) produce training materials: printed handouts, in-store posters, social media promotional graphics
Responsible (R): Marketing Events Coordinator
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 16 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1260_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1260_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1260_Task6" name="Monthly calendar publication &amp; registration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Monthly calendar publication &amp; registration: (a) publish next month&#x27;s workshop calendar: in-store poster, website event page, social media event, email to loyalty members; (b) open online registration via buildright.com.ph — loyalty members get priority registration; (c) set capacity limits per workshop (15–20 attendees) with waitlist; (d) send reminder notifications 3 days and 1 day before workshop; (e) provide Store Manager with attendee list and materials list for preparation
Responsible (R): Marketing Events Coordinator
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1260_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1260_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1260_Task7" name="Workshop execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Workshop execution: Sales Associate conducts workshop in designated store area (power tool demo zone or paint mixing station): (a) set up workshop area with materials, tools, and seating; (b) present project tutorial — demonstrate technique, assist attendees with hands-on practice; (c) promote related products during workshop — &quot;everything you need is in Aisle 7&quot;; (d) offer workshop-exclusive discount (10–15% off featured materials) valid for 24 hours; (e) scan attendee loyalty cards for attendance tracking and post-event follow-up
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Supplier Representative
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 90 min per workshop</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1260_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1260_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1260_Task8" name="Post-event measurement &amp; follow-up">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Post-event measurement &amp; follow-up: Within 1 week of workshop: (a) system tracks post-workshop purchase uplift: attendee purchases of featured category in 14-day window vs. non-attendee control group; (b) send attendee satisfaction survey (CSAT + NPS) via email/SMS; (c) add attendee to DIY workshop email segment for future events; (d) compile monthly workshop performance report: attendance rate, CSAT, purchase uplift, cost per attendee; (e) share results with Category Managers and VP Marketing
Responsible (R): Marketing Events Coordinator / BI Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1260_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1260_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1260_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1260_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1260_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-281 (ensure controlled execution — Campaign Planning &amp; Execution (PA-14.1).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Marketing Events Coordinator</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
