    <bpmn:process id="W_W1270" name="W1270. Seasonal Promotional Catalog Production, Printing &amp; Store Distribution" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Bi-monthly promotional calendar event (6 major catalog-based promotions per year per §13.3)
Frequency: 6 catalogs/year (bi-monthly: Jan–Feb, Mar–Apr, May–Jun, Jul–Aug, Sep–Oct, Nov–Dec)
Volume: ~200 printed copies per store × 200 stores = ~40,000 copies per catalog + digital version for ecommerce and social media
Owner: Marketing Manager
Participants: Marketing Manager, Category Managers (5), VP Merchandising, In-House Designer, Print Vendor, Store Operations Coordinator, Ecommerce Ops
Source: workflow W1270 — Seasonal Promotional Catalog Production, Printing &amp; Store Distribution</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1270_LaneSet8">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1270_Lane1" name="Marketing Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1270_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1270_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1270_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1270_Start9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1270_Lane2" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1270_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1270_Lane3" name="In-House Designer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1270_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1270_Lane4" name="Ecommerce Ops">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1270_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1270_Lane5" name="Store Operations Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1270_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1270_Lane6" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1270_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1270_Lane7" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1270_Task18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1270_End19</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1270_Start9" name="Bi-monthly promotional calendar event (6 major catalog-based promotions per year per…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1270_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1270_Task10" name="Catalog item selection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Catalog item selection: 6 weeks before catalog effective date, Marketing Manager facilitates item selection meeting with Category Managers: (a) each Category Manager proposes 5–8 items per category based on: seasonal relevance (§13.2), margin uplift potential, vendor co-op funding availability (W738), inventory position (overstock items prioritized for clearance), competitive pricing intelligence (W130), (b) Marketing Manager curates final item list of 20–40 SKUs with balanced category representation, (c) VP Merchandising approves final catalog item list and promotional pricing per W13
Responsible (R): Marketing Manager / Category Managers
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1 day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1270_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1270_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1270_Task11" name="Vendor co-op funding confirmation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Vendor co-op funding confirmation: for each catalog item with vendor-funded promotion, Category Manager confirms with vendor: (a) co-op advertising contribution amount, (b) markdown allowance per unit, (c) minimum volume commitment, (d) vendor logo/branding requirements; confirmed items flagged in system for W738 trade fund tracking
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): Marketing Manager
Duration: 3–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1270_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1270_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1270_Task12" name="Creative brief and design">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Creative brief and design: In-House Designer creates catalog based on approved item list: (a) layout templates standardized across catalogs (cover, category pages, back cover with store locator), (b) product photography — new shots for featured items; existing product images from PIM (W50) for standard items, (c) pricing display: original price (strikethrough), promotional price, savings amount, percentage off, (d) seasonal theme design aligned with promotional calendar (e.g., summer: garden and outdoor theme; ber-months: holiday colors), (e) QR codes linking to ecommerce product pages, (f) store-specific variants: regional price differences or item availability variations handled through versioned pages
Responsible (R): In-House Designer
Accountable (A): Marketing Manager
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1270_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1270_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1270_Task13" name="Legal and compliance review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Legal and compliance review: Marketing Manager reviews catalog for: (a) BIR compliance — all prices include VAT (12%), price display per Consumer Act (RA 7394) requirements, (b) DTI compliance — promotional pricing rules (original price must have been offered for at least 30 days in prior 90-day period), (c) senior citizen/PWD discount eligibility notation where applicable, (d) accurate product specifications and images — no misleading claims, (e) correct terms and conditions (sale period dates, return policy during promotions)
Responsible (R): Marketing Manager
Accountable (A): Legal Counsel (if needed)
Duration: 2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1270_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1270_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1270_Task14" name="Print production">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Print production: once design approved: (a) Marketing Manager sends print-ready files to contracted print vendor, (b) print specifications: A4 or A5 format, 8–16 pages, matte cover + gloss interior, ~50,000 copies (200 per store = 40,000 + 5,000 for direct mail to top trade accounts + 5,000 for loyalty member mailings), (c) print vendor provides proof for final approval before full run, (d) production timeline: 7–10 business days from proof approval
Responsible (R): Marketing Manager / Print Vendor
Accountable (A): Marketing Manager
Duration: 7–10 days (vendor)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1270_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1270_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1270_Task15" name="Digital catalog production">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Digital catalog production: parallel to print production, Ecommerce Ops prepares digital version: (a) catalog uploaded to buildright.com.ph as browsable flipbook, (b) individual product pages updated with promotional pricing and catalog badge, (c) social media assets created from catalog design — carousel posts, stories, and paid ad creatives, (d) email marketing template with catalog highlights for loyalty member segments, (e) mobile push notification with catalog link for app users
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Ops / In-House Designer
Accountable (A): Marketing Manager
Duration: 3–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1270_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1270_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1270_Task16" name="Logistics and store distribution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Logistics and store distribution: printed catalogs shipped to 4 DCs alongside regular store replenishment: (a) print vendor delivers to DC1 (Davao) and DC3 (Calamba) for regional distribution, (b) each store receives 200 copies bundled in protective wrapping, (c) Store Operations Coordinator communicates catalog arrival dates and display instructions to Store Managers: (i) catalog display rack at store entrance, (ii) copies at checkout counters, (iii) copies at customer service counter for trade account customers, (iv) copies in department sections for category-specific items
Responsible (R): Store Operations Coordinator / DC Logistics
Accountable (A): Marketing Manager
Duration: 3–5 days (shipping)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1270_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1270_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1270_Task17" name="In-store catalog deployment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: In-store catalog deployment: Store Manager ensures catalogs are displayed by effective date: (a) catalog display rack placed at store entrance per visual merchandising guidelines, (b) Sales Associates briefed on catalog items and promotional pricing in daily huddle (W5), (c) promotional shelf tags and signage installed per W262, (d) Department Supervisors verify price accuracy at POS for all catalog items
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Department Supervisors
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1270_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1270_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1270_Task18" name="Post-campaign catalog disposition">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Post-campaign catalog disposition: at end of promotional period: (a) remaining catalogs collected from displays and checkout counters, (b) catalogs with future-relevant content retained for customer reference rack, (c) outdated catalogs recycled; Store Manager reports unsold catalog count to Marketing for print quantity optimization in next cycle
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30 min/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1270_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1270_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1270_End19" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1270_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1270_Annotation20">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-281 (ensure controlled execution — Campaign Planning &amp; Execution (PA-14.1).) | - operational: Marketing Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Marketing Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1270_Assoc21" sourceRef="W1270_Annotation20" targetRef="W1270_Start9" associationDirection="None" />
