    <bpmn:process id="W_W1292" name="W1292. Seasonal Builder&#x27;s Expo &amp; Community Event Planning" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual seasonal event calendar planning; or regional opportunity for community engagement event
Frequency: 2–3 major Builder&#x27;s Expos per year (pre-summer, pre-Ber months, post-typhoon renovation); 1 community event per store per quarter
Volume: ~2–3 major regional/national expos; ~200 community events per quarter across all stores
Owner: Marketing Events Coordinator
Participants: Marketing Events Coordinator, Store Manager, Category Manager, Vendor Partners, Sales Associates, Local Government (LGU)
Source: workflow W1292 — Seasonal Builder&#x27;s Expo &amp; Community Event Planning</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1292_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1292_Lane1" name="Marketing Events Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1292_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1292_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1292_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1292_Lane2" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1292_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1292_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1292_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1292_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1292_Lane4" name="Marketing">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1292_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1292_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1292_Start6" name="Annual seasonal event calendar planning; or regional opportunity for community engagement…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1292_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1292_Task7" name="Annual event calendar planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Annual event calendar planning: Marketing Events Coordinator develops annual event calendar aligned with seasonal calendar per W264: (a) Pre-Summer Builder&#x27;s Expo (Feb–Mar): focus on new construction materials, aircon, garden, (b) Post-Typhoon Renovation Expo (Aug–Sep): waterproofing, repair materials, emergency supplies, (c) Holiday Home Makeover Expo (Oct–Nov): Christmas décor, appliances, paint, furniture, (d) coordinate with Category Managers for vendor participation and co-op funding per W262, (e) confirm venue (in-store, parking lot, or partnered venue) and budget per event
Responsible (R): Marketing Events Coordinator
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 8 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1292_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1292_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1292_Task8" name="Vendor participation coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Vendor participation coordination: Category Manager invites key vendors to participate: (a) confirm vendor booth/demo space requirements, (b) negotiate co-op marketing funding (vendors typically fund 50–70% of event costs for their category), (c) arrange vendor product samples, demonstration units, and promotional pricing for event duration, (d) coordinate vendor logistics (delivery of display materials, setup/teardown schedule), (e) for major expos: coordinate with vendor national accounts for maximum participation
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Vendor
Accountable (A): Marketing Events Coordinator
Duration: 4 hours/event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1292_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1292_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1292_Task9" name="LGU &amp; community coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: LGU &amp; community coordination: For community events: (a) Store Manager coordinates with local barangay captain or LGU for event partnership, (b) obtain necessary permits for outdoor events per W446, (c) arrange LGU participation (local officials as event guests, community project dedications), (d) coordinate with local emergency services (fire department, police) for event safety per W440, (e) for school build-out events: partner with local school for material donation per W1106
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Marketing Events Coordinator
Duration: 4 hours/event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1292_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1292_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1292_Task10" name="Marketing &amp; promotion">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Marketing &amp; promotion: Marketing executes event promotion: (a) digital marketing per W14.2: social media event pages, targeted ads to loyalty members within 10 km radius, email to trade account customers, (b) in-store: event posters, shelf talkers, PA system announcements, (c) SMS blast to loyalty members per tier (Gold/Platinum: VIP early access), (d) local radio or community newspaper ads for major expos, (e) coordinate with vendor partners for cross-promotion on vendor channels
Responsible (R): Marketing
Accountable (A): Marketing Events Coordinator
Duration: 8 hours/event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1292_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1292_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1292_Task11" name="Event day execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Event day execution: Store Manager and team execute event: (a) setup: vendor booths, demonstration areas, event stage, signage, PA system, (b) Sales Associates staffed at high-traffic positions for customer engagement, (c) loyalty enrollment booth for new member sign-ups, (d) trade account sign-up desk for contractor registration per W24, (e) Customer Service Rep manages information and complaint desk, (f) Department Supervisors monitor crowd safety and vendor compliance per W440, (g) real-time social media coverage (photos, live videos) per W14.2
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Sales Associates
Accountable (A): Marketing Events Coordinator
Duration: 8–12 hours/event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1292_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1292_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1292_Task12" name="Post-event analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Post-event analysis: Marketing Events Coordinator compiles post-event report: (a) foot traffic vs. baseline (target: 2–3x normal weekend), (b) sales lift by category during event, (c) new loyalty sign-ups and trade account registrations, (d) vendor satisfaction feedback, (e) customer feedback and social media engagement, (f) event cost vs. incremental revenue (ROI), (g) lessons learned and recommendations for next event
Responsible (R): Marketing Events Coordinator
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 4 hours/event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1292_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1292_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1292_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1292_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1292_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-281 (ensure controlled execution — Campaign Planning &amp; Execution (PA-14.1).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Marketing Events Coordinator</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1292_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1292_Annotation14" targetRef="W1292_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
