    <bpmn:process id="W_W1523" name="W1523. New Store Grand Opening Marketing Campaign, Local Launch Event &amp; Community Introduction" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New store construction completed and target opening date confirmed (per PA-20.2 Engineering &amp; Construction)
Frequency: ~10–15 new store openings/year based on the expansion plan (per profile §3.1)
Volume: 1 store per grand opening event; local population within 10-km radius = 50,000–200,000 people
Owner: Marketing Communications Manager
Participants: Marketing Comms Manager, Store Manager (designate), VP Store Operations, LGU officials, Category Managers, local media
Source: workflow W1523 — New Store Grand Opening Marketing Campaign, Local Launch Event &amp; Community Introduction</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1523_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1523_Lane1" name="Marketing Comms Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1523_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1523_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1523_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1523_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1523_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1523_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1523_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1523_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1523_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1523_Start4" name="New store construction completed and target opening date confirmed (per PA-20.2…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1523_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1523_Task5" name="Pre-opening planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Pre-opening planning (8–12 weeks before opening): (a) Marketing Communications Manager develops grand opening plan: (i) target opening date (coordinated with real estate and construction teams per PA-20.2), (ii) budget allocation (PHP 500K–1.5M per opening: event setup, advertising, promotional items, giveaways), (iii) marketing channels: local radio, barangay flyers, social media (Facebook community groups), local newspaper, tarpaulin/billboard near store, jeepney/tricycle ads; (b) coordinates with Store Manager (designate) on: (i) store readiness timeline, (ii) staffing readiness (all 29 positions filled per PA-19.1), (iii) initial inventory fully merchandised; (c) obtains necessary LGU permits for outdoor event setup, sound system, temporary signage
Responsible (R): Marketing Comms Manager / Store Manager (designate)
Accountable (A): VP Marketing / VP Store Operations
Duration: 2–3 weeks planning</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1523_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1523_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1523_Task6" name="Community and LGU engagement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Community and LGU engagement (6–8 weeks before opening): (a) Store Manager (designate) and Marketing Communications Manager conduct courtesy calls on: (i) Municipal/City Mayor — invite as guest of honor for ribbon-cutting, brief on BuildRight&#x27;s community investment and local employment; (ii) Barangay Captain(s) of surrounding barangays — invite to opening, discuss community partnerships; (iii) Local DTI office — ensure business permit and consumer protection compliance; (b) build local contractor/trade professional prospect list: partner with local hardware stores (potential customers for BuildRight&#x27;s trade program per VS-11) and construction associations
Responsible (R): Store Manager (designate) / Marketing Comms Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1523_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1523_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1523_Task7" name="Pre-opening marketing blitz">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Pre-opening marketing blitz (4–2 weeks before opening): (a) execute multi-channel advertising: (i) local radio spots (2–3 stations, 30-second spots, 10x/day for 2 weeks), (ii) 50,000 flyers door-to-door within 5-km radius via barangay distribution network, (iii) Facebook geo-targeted ads within 10-km radius, (iv) tarpaulin signage on major roads leading to store, (v) local newspaper half-page ad; (b) content messaging: (i) &quot;BuildRight Depot is Coming to [City]!&quot; with store photo/render, (ii) grand opening promo teaser (e.g., &quot;First 500 customers get a free BuildRight tote bag!&quot;), (iii) &quot;Now Hiring&quot; if positions still open; (c) grand opening flyer produced per W1522 process with opening-day exclusive deals
Responsible (R): Marketing Comms Manager / Graphic Designer
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 2 weeks execution</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1523_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1523_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1523_Task8" name="VIP and trade pre-opening event">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: VIP and trade pre-opening event (1–2 days before public opening): (a) private preview event for: (i) LGU officials and guests, (ii) local contractors and trade professionals (invite to join BuildRight trade program per W1507), (iii) media (local TV, newspaper, radio); (b) Store Manager gives store tour; Category Managers present key product categories; (c) light refreshments and entertainment; (d) purpose: build relationships, generate media coverage, and pre-sign trade accounts before public opening
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Marketing Comms Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: Half-day event + 2 days prep</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1523_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1523_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1523_Task9" name="Grand opening day execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Grand opening day execution: (a) ceremonial ribbon-cutting by Mayor/Barangay Captain with BuildRight executives; (b) store opens to public; (c) opening day activities: (i) first 500 customers receive free gift (tote bag, tape measure, or BuildRight voucher), (ii) hourly raffle prizes (power tools, paint sets, gift certificates), (iii) live product demonstrations (paint mixing, lumber cutting, tile estimation — per PA-09.1/09.2), (iv) children&#x27;s activity area (to keep families in-store longer), (v) food stalls from local vendors (community partnership); (d) Store Manager and team manage customer flow, ensure checkout queues are managed (all 3 POS terminals active); (e) Marketing Communications Manager coordinates media coverage: photo opportunities, customer testimonials, social media live posts
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Marketing Comms Manager / All Store Staff
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: Full-day event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1523_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1523_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1523_Task10" name="Post-opening follow-up">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Post-opening follow-up (30 days after opening): (a) Marketing Communications Manager tracks: (i) opening week sales vs. target, (ii) new customer registrations (loyalty sign-ups), (iii) trade account openings, (iv) social media engagement metrics, (v) local media coverage value; (b) Store Manager conducts 30-day review: customer feedback, product gaps, staffing adjustments; (c) transition from grand opening marketing to steady-state local marketing per W1522 (monthly flyer) and VS-14 marketing operations
Responsible (R): Marketing Comms Manager / Store Manager
Accountable (A): VP Marketing / VP Store Operations
Duration: 4–6 hours analysis</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1523_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1523_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1523_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1523_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1523_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-281 (ensure controlled execution — Campaign Planning &amp; Execution (PA-14.1).) | - operational: Marketing Communications Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Marketing Communications Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1523_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1523_Annotation12" targetRef="W1523_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1523_Flow14" sourceRef="W1523_Start4" targetRef="W1523_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1523_Flow15" sourceRef="W1523_Task5" targetRef="W1523_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1523_Flow16" sourceRef="W1523_Task6" targetRef="W1523_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1523_Flow17" sourceRef="W1523_Task7" targetRef="W1523_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1523_Flow18" sourceRef="W1523_Task8" targetRef="W1523_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1523_Flow19" sourceRef="W1523_Task9" targetRef="W1523_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1523_Flow20" sourceRef="W1523_Task10" targetRef="W1523_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
